-      "requirements": "# Puzzle Punks Unity art reuse and export handoff\n\nThe core art for the Tropical Island, Punk-a-thon, puzzles, difficulty presentation, and Jest marketing surfaces is already in this Unity project. Reuse and composition are the default plan; a new commission is optional only for a deliberate art-direction change.\n\n## Jest platform artwork — compose and export existing Unity art\n\n| Deliverable | Existing Unity source | Remaining work |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1:1 store-listing image | `Assets/Art/Temp/Textures/AppIcon_Google.png`, alternate `AppIcon-Dash.png`, and `Assets/Art/UI/PuzzlePunksLogo.png` | Select the approved composition and export the Developer Console crop. |\n| 16:9 store-listing hero | 4316×4096 `Assets/Art/UI/LoadingScreenBG.jpg`, the separated splash layers below, and the authored Tropical scene | Compose/crop a flattened 16:9 export; no new character or environment source art is required. |\n| 3:2 notification master | `Assets/Art/UI/image_notifications.png`, logo, key visual, and splash layers | Compose a readable notification-size export and submit it for platform approval. |\n| Referral/share card | The same key visual, logo, and character layers | Export PNG, JPEG, or WebP at no more than 2 MB. |\n\nThe existing separated 2048×2048 splash composition is already wired into `LaunchScreen.prefab`:\n\n- `Assets/Art/UI/PP_Splash_BG1.png`\n- `Assets/Art/UI/PP_Splash_BG2.png`\n- `Assets/Art/UI/PP_Splash_BG3.png`\n- `Assets/Art/UI/PP_Splash_BG4a.png`\n- `Assets/Art/UI/PP_Splash_Logo.png`\n\nThese PNG layers provide editable separation for background, distant characters, foreground characters/tiles, framing foliage, and logo. There is no PSD/PSB in the repository; request the approved layered master from the art drive only if one already exists or production specifically requires that format.\n\nExport rules:\n\n- Keep the logo, Punk faces, and main action within a central crop-safe area.\n- Avoid small baked-in copy and do not include prices, player data, or time-sensitive promotions.\n- Preserve the Unity source files; create platform-specific flattened exports rather than overwriting them.\n- Upload the approved results to the Jest Developer Console asset library. Until notification art is approved, Jest uses the configured Hero image as its fallback.\n\n## Tropical Island gameplay parity — existing Unity art integrated\n\nThe Tropical scene now uses the project’s existing authored art and preserves the exact runtime identifiers:\n\n- **Match cone light** — `Cone_light_prefab.prefab` supplies the four visible cone meshes. The existing podium-centred Spot Light remains the functional light. Both sit under the inactive `TropicalConeLight` wrapper controlled by `SceneLightingController`.\n- **Punk-a-thon route** — `Race` and its closed 24-point `SplineSupport` are scene configuration, not a missing track model. The spline is fitted around Tropical’s central lagoon while the authored island paths and terrain remain the visible route.\n- **Finish line and winner staging** — `End_sign.prefab` supplies the wood/checkered gate and its existing `Logo` material locator. `FinishRaceHangout` is an authored Tropical staging transform, not separate art.\n- **Static race view** — `PunkAThonStaticView` is an authored Tropical camera-position marker framing the central podiums and background environment.\n- **Celebration VFX** — `Fireworks_largeExplosionsAllColours.prefab` supplies all five particle systems. The root remains active so its `SceneObject` registers, while every particle system remains dormant until results trigger it.\n\nAuthoritative reusable assets:\n\n- `Assets/Art/Temp/Environments/Night_Island/Prefabs/End_sign.prefab`\n- `Assets/Art/Temp/Environments/Night_Island/Prefabs/Cone_light_prefab.prefab`\n- `Assets/Art/Temp/Vfx/Fireworks/Fireworks_largeExplosionsAllColours.prefab`\n- `Assets/Art/Temp/Environments/Tropical_Island/` (complete Tropical meshes, textures, materials, shaders, and VFX)\n\nNo external Tropical race-art files are required.\n\n## Other art already available\n\n- Twelve exact Punk poses and names from the skin wheel, configured in `Assets/Resources/Config/ImagePuzzleCatalog.asset`.\n- `Assets/Art/UI/RewardsMap/bgRewardsMap.png` for the multi-puzzle presentation.\n- Hard and Extreme carousel art plus both dedicated pre-match overlays.\n- Six local gem reward images and twelve Punk reward portraits under `Assets/ProgressiveContentResources/UI/Rewards/`.\n- Complete shop chrome including `bgShop.png`, pack bases, dividers, and icons.\n\n## Remote shop cards not stored locally\n\nCurrent shop configuration references fourteen image basenames that are not in Unity or Git history:\n\n- `ELP.png`\n- `skinWheel.png`, `tileWheel.png`, `luckyWheel2.png`, `dailyGemWheel.png`\n- `StarterPack.png`, `ShopSkinDeal.png`, `ShopCyberPack.png`\n- `tiles_magic.png`, `tiles_bakery.png`, `tiles_punk.png`, `tiles_fruit.png`, `tiles_pixel.png`, `tiles_plastic.png`\n\nThese are downloaded at runtime from the configured CDN by `SessionBasedImageCacheService`; their repository absence does not prove that the live CDN is missing them. Request the approved originals from the art drive only if a self-contained/local fallback is required or CDN validation shows a real missing file. Existing wheel, ELP, tileset, shop, and character assets can be recomposed internally if no approved originals exist.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Verify the Tropical race route, winner lineup, static view, cone transition, finish-logo material swap, and result fireworks in Unity.\n- Test the scene on representative Android and iOS hardware before release.\n- Test Jest listing crops, notification fallback, and a real referral preview after Console upload.\n- Keep imported source art and `.meta` files together; add exports through the appropriate asset/addressable collection rather than hard-coded filesystem loading.\n\n## References\n\n- [Jest SDK changes: listing crops, notification ratio, and referral image limits](https://docs.jest.com/whats-new)\n- [Jest notifications](https://docs.jest.com/sdk/unity/notifications)\n- [Jest referrals](https://docs.jest.com/sdk/unity/referrals)\n- [Jest launch checklist](https://docs.jest.com/launch-checklist)\n"
