e Tropical meshes, textures, materials, shaders, and VFX)\n\nNo external Tropical race-art files are required.\n\n## Other art already available\n\n- Twelve exact Punk poses and names from the skin wheel, configured in `Assets/Resources/Config/ImagePuzzleCatalog.asset`.\n- `Assets/Art/UI/RewardsMap/bgRewardsMap.png` for the multi-puzzle presentation.\n- Hard and Extreme carousel art plus both dedicated pre-match overlays.\n- Six local gem reward images and twelve Punk reward portraits under `Assets/ProgressiveContentResources/UI/Rewards/`.\n- Complete shop chrome including `bgShop.png`, pack bases, dividers, and icons.\n\n## Remote shop cards not stored locally\n\nCurrent shop configuration references fourteen image basenames that are not in Unity or Git history:\n\n- `ELP.png`\n- `skinWheel.png`, `tileWheel.png`, `luckyWheel2.png`, `dailyGemWheel.png`\n- `StarterPack.png`, `ShopSkinDeal.png`, `ShopCyberPack.png`\n- `tiles_magic.png`, `tiles_bakery.png`, `tiles_punk.png`, `tiles_fruit.png`, `tiles_pixel.png`, `tiles_plastic.png`\n\nThese are downloaded at runtime from the configured CDN by `SessionBasedImageCacheService`; their repository absence does not prove that the live CDN is missing them. Request the approved originals from the art drive only if a self-contained/local fallback is required or CDN validation shows a real missing file. Existing wheel, ELP, tileset, shop, and character assets can be recomposed internally if no approved originals exist.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Verify the Tropical race route, winner lineup, static view, cone transition, finish-logo material swap, and result fireworks in Unity.\n- Test the scene on representative Android and iOS hardware before release.\n- Test Jest listing crops, notification fallback, and a real referral preview after Console upload.\n- Keep imported source art and `.meta` files together; add exports through the appropriate asset/addressable collection rather than hard-coded filesystem loading.\n\n## References\n\n-