c7dfa66f`, SHA-256 `663310448bfbb4a7784423f282b51fa90707040df24d9912752e3e680430666a`) is ready and inactive. Scanning the decompressed WebGL data, framework, and WebAssembly found no Stripe domain, Stripe integration, EssentialKit billing, or `BillingServices` string. A direct-host startup made no Stripe network request and produced no browser error. Jest payment tests pass 35/35; native fulfillment tests pass 18/18 under the iOS target and 17/17 under Android; the platform-SKU selector assertion passes in both runs. Android and iOS player-script compilation both pass.\n\n## Authoritative review state\n\nRetrieved through the Jest MCP `get_game_details` tool for Puzzle Punks (`019f0e39-7bf3-70b2-92ac-6f67161af265`).\n\n- Game is unpublished; no submission is currently in review.\n- Latest rejection refers to the submission dated `2026-09-17T05:28:37.419Z`.\n- Current active draft build: `1.6.5-dev.26267145651`, version ID `01a0d3f0-20af-764a-8ad8-71f8af250788`.\n- This is a development-backend build. Production-backend readiness must be verified separately before a production release.\n- The player-feedback endpoint returned no additional items. The reviewer\u2019s attached screenshots still need to be inspected in the authenticated Console; the MCP review text does not include them.\n\n## Required remediation and evidence\n\nThe 2026-09-24 remediation build `1.6.5-dev.26267145651` (version ID\n`01a0d3f0-20af-764a-8ad8-71f8af250788`, SHA-256\n`66c671d748261bb5628d71142becd9440a02c8f316fb2b63b2cc224b2cf259a7`) is ready\nand active on the unpublished draft. It contains the fixes below. The rows remain open until the required\nphysical-device and gameplay evidence is captured from this exact candidate.\n\n- J01 uses Jest's maintained login UI instead of the custom registration chrome.\n- J02 keeps the carousel trophy layer as the top UI sibling above opponent avatars.\n- J03 removes the `parasol` camera/spawn candidate that placed the player inside\n  the sun-lounger collision volume.\n- J04 anchors the Live action controls to the bottom safe edge instead of a fixed\n  `-914` offset.\n- J05 derives knock-down star placement from the losing character's visible bounds.\n- J06 removes the `bar_table_chairs` camera candidate whose sightline crosses the\n  `water_uv` and `water_uv1` meshes.\n- J07 keeps the base head visible when a skin references a missing custom-head prop.\n- J08 always displays the numeric IQ score, including the valid starting score of 0.\n- J09 follows the browser visual viewport during toolbar resize and restricts native\n  autorotation to portrait.\n- J10 explicitly tells the player to tap the rocket and bomb to activate them; the\n  first drop tutorial already says `TAP TO DROP TILES`.\n\nAutomated evidence for this source revision: 374 Edit Mode tests passed with one\nexisting ignored test, the focused loading-service Play Mode tests passed 11/11,\nand the earlier full 560-test Play Mode and focused layout/environment/effect/head\nsuites passed before the logging-only follow-up. A 390x844 Jest-hosted launch kept\nthe Welcome prompt inside the viewport, completed in 6.367 seconds, and produced\nno browser page errors. The SDK mock bridge does not close any authenticated,\nphysical-device, or gameplay row.\n\n| ID | Reviewer finding | Required verification before closing |\n|---|---|---|\n| J01 | Registration close button overlaps text | Open the guest registration panel on narrow and tall mobile viewports. Capture readable copy, a separate close target, and successful dismissal. |\n| J02 | Monkey overlaps trophies | Capture the main menu with the monkey equipped; all trophy values and controls must remain visible. |\n| J03 | Monkey stands inside the chair after returning from a level | Start from the menu, finish a level, and return. Record the character returning to the intended seated pose without intersecting the chair. Repeat the transition. |\n| J04 | Live start button is offscreen | Enter Live and its start/lobby states on mobile. Capture the entire button within the visible safe area and demonstrate that it can be tapped. |\n| J05 | Victory stars spin in front of / through the opponent | Complete a match and record the whole victory animation. Verify effect positioning and rendering against both characters. |\n| J06 | Water renders over the character\u2019s head | Reproduce the reviewer\u2019s environment and camera state. Record water rendering correctly before and after gameplay transitions. |\n| J07 | A skin has no head | Identify the skin from the review attachment. Verify its preview, equipped menu appearance, gameplay, and return-to-menu state; check the remaining selectable skins as well. |\n| J08 | IQ is `n/a` with no explanation of how to obtain a rating | With an unrated account, verify clear explanatory text and an accessible explanation of the actual rating requirements. Verify the rated state after the backend awards a rating. |\n| J09 | Game content goes offscreen | Check menu, registration, shop, profile, Live, gameplay, and results on narrow/tall viewports, including browser toolbar resizing. No essential text or interactive control may be clipped. |\n| J10 | Tutorial does not explain tapping to place blocks or breaking bombs/rockets | Use a fresh account and record a first-time walkthrough that teaches placement and both special-block mechanics before they are required. Verify the user can perform the explained actions. |\n| J11 | The game works in Jest's Simulator but startup fails on physical devices (reported on two devices and two browsers) | Reproduce using the reviewer\u2019s device/browser details when available. Record cold launches on physical Android Chrome and iOS Safari, including console/runtime failure evidence. Compare the first failing stage with the passing Simulator run. Browser emulation alone does not close this item. |\n| J12 | Simulator loading takes 11\u201313 seconds | Measure cold-cache navigation to genuinely interactive gameplay/menu on a documented standard mobile connection. Each required device must meet the published under-10-second requirement. Capture timings, network conditions, and artifact identity. |\n| J13 | Ten-minute stability could not be assessed because startup failed | After J11 passes, record at least ten minutes of active gameplay and transitions on each required mobile browser. Include responsiveness, errors, memory observations, and final state. An idle document-ready check alone is insufficient. |\n\n## Current verification blocker\n\nThe following hosted check was run against the exact active draft on 2026-09-22:\n\n```bash\ncd Tools/JestSandboxValidation\nJEST_GAME_URL='https://jest.com/g/puzzle-punks?versionId=01a0abe9-2934-7658-acc0-7561d3525ed4' \\\nJEST_GUEST_STORAGE_STATE=\"$PWD/../../IgnoredByGit/jest-registered-state.json\" \\\nnpx playwright test --project=android-chrome --grep 'account identity'\n```\n\nResult: **failed after 7.6 seconds at the authorization check**, with `403` and `This app isn't public yet`. This is an access failure, not a reproduced game crash or a load-time measurement. The Console also redirects to sign-in. `adb devices` reports no connected devices.\n\nRestore an authorized developer/sandbox session and connect the Android device; obtain physical iOS Safari access and the reviewer attachments before closing the corresponding items. Keep login state, traces, and account data in ignored local paths.\n\n## Resubmission evidence\n\nFor each resolved item, record the reproduction, fix commit, exact candidate version and artifact SHA-256, device/browser/viewport, verification date, and evidence path. Re-run the automated Basic Launch checks and purchase recovery on that same candidate. Resolve every row before activating and submitting, then verify that Jest reports the new version in review. Do not describe an accepted upload as a review submission or publication.\n\nReferences: [Jest launch checklist](https://docs.jest.com/launch-checklist), [review and moderation](https://docs.jest.com/content-review-and-moderation), [build management](https://docs.jest.com/dev-console/builds).\n"
