-      "requirements": "# The Hive\n\nRun development, tests and deployment from this `BeeHive` folder. Backend code lives in `backend/hive/`. The separate Puzzle Punks repository, including its Git history, lives in `backend/puzzle-punks/`; `Documents/backend` is a shortcut to it. The older Hive app is preserved in a private archive under `_backups/consolidation-20261008/`. See [the consolidation notes](docs/CONSOLIDATION.md).\n\nThe Hive (working name Buzz TV) is a quiz game for Factory International's learning hub (Titus, on Moodle), where every learner grows a bee from their answers.\n\n1. **Build Your Bee.** The home page shows a starter bee and an editable, made-up name. Learners can keep that name or invent their own, then select **Next**. There are no skin unlocks or Random Bee option.\n2. **Discover Your Transferable Skills.** Selecting **Next** opens the first question of the 15-question career profile, with no category choice and no right or wrong answers. As learners answer, their bee grows on a retro TV. Its costume, prop, wing pattern, stripes and glow relate to their answers.\n3. **Join The Hive.** Their finished bee joins the live swarm shown full screen on a TV in the building. Playing again on the same device can rename and regrow the same bee, and the TV updates its name and design.\n\nBee names must have 2 to 24 Unicode characters, start with a letter, and use letters, digits, spaces, apostrophes or hyphens. The server validates and moderates them through `POST /api/bee-name` before the quiz starts, and checks them again before publication. Learners should invent names rather than use real names. Plays are anonymous, and Moodle does not send learner details to the Hive.\n\nOptional AI agents, written by Claude, switch on when `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is set: a **host bee** that comments on the Hive TV, a **career coach** with personal next steps on the results screen, **Draft with AI** for admins, and AI bees that fill the Hive while it has fewer than 30 real bees. Without a key, everything works with hand-written text. See [docs/HANDOFF.md section 9](docs/HANDOFF.md#9-the-ai-agents-claude).\n\n| Page | Live address | What it is |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/` | https://buzz-tv-six.vercel.app | The game. Moodle shows this, through the SCORM package or an iframe. |\n| `/tv` | https://buzz-tv-six.vercel.app/tv | The Hive TV. Open it full screen on the laptop connected to the TV. |\n| `/admin` | https://buzz-tv-six.vercel.app/admin | Admin: questions, bees, stats and admins. Log in with an email one-time link (approved emails only). |\n\n**Read the full hand-off guide: [docs/HANDOFF.md](docs/HANDOFF.md).** It covers admin how-tos, Moodle set-up, the Hive TV, the logo and fonts, deployment, the database, security and known issues. For step-by-step Totara and Moodle set-up, see [docs/LMS-SETUP.md](docs/LMS-SETUP.md). Content checks are in [docs/CONTENT-QA.md](docs/CONTENT-QA.md).\n\nProject tasks and requirements are in the [shared dashboard](https://roobsworld.com/dashboard). See [the task dashboard guide](docs/TASK-DASHBOARD.md) for direct AI API access and refresh commands.\n\n## How it's built\n\n- Plain Node 20+, with static HTML, CSS and JavaScript in `public/` (no build step). The only npm dependency is the official Anthropic SDK, for the optional AI bees.\n- One Vercel function (`api/index.js`, which uses `backend/hive/handler.js`) serves every `/api/*` route.\n- Supabase stores questions, bees, anonymous plays and admins. Only the server talks to it.\n- `npm run build:scorm` makes a small SCORM 1.2 launcher (`dist/the-hive-scorm12.zip`). It shows the live site inside Moodle and reports results.\n\n## Quick start for developers\n\n```bash\nnpm run dev          # http://localhost:3000 (game /, Hive TV /tv, admin /admin)\nnpm test             # Node test runner, in-memory data\nnpm run build:scorm  # dist/the-hive-scorm12.zip; add -- --pass 70 for pass/fail\n```\n\n- `npm run dev` explicitly enables disposable memory storage when neither Supabase setting is present. Hosted deployments and partial credentials fail closed with 503.\n- Admin login then returns a local dev token instead of emailing a link. Use `grindheadgames@gmail.com`, the built-in owner.\n- If `.env` has `SUPABASE_URL` and `SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY`, the local server uses that Supabase project instead.\n\nCopy `.env.example` to `.env` for the variable names. Their meanings are in [docs/HANDOFF.md section 7.4](docs/HANDOFF.md#74-environment-variables). Never commit `.env`.\n\n## Deploy\n\n```bash\nnpm run deploy\n```\n\nThis deploys the Hive to the existing Vercel project `buzz-tv`, using its configured production environment. Then check that `/api/health` shows `\"storage\":\"supabase\"`. To replace environment settings from `.env`, update Supabase login URLs and rebuild the SCORM package, use `bash scripts/deploy-now.sh`.\n\nFor a new database, run the SQL files in `supabase/` in this order: `01`, `03`, `02`, `04`, `05`, `06`, `07`, `08`, `09`, `10`, `11`. See [docs/HANDOFF.md section 7.6](docs/HANDOFF.md#76-database-set-up-and-migrations).\n\n## Content\n\nWebsite wording can be edited in a Google Sheet with `Header` and `Content` columns. The game, Hive TV, admin interface, quiz wording and results read the mapping through `/api/content`. See [the website text guide](docs/WEBSITE-TEXT.md) for connection settings, refresh behavior and adding new question rows.\n\n- The career quiz is the client's Creative Career Discovery content (`backend/hive/career-discovery-questions.json`), scored by `backend/hive/career.js`.\n- The four arts quizzes (Theatre, Music, Dance and Visual Art) are in `backend/hive/seed-data.js` and remain editable in admin and available through the API. The learner website shows the transferable skills quiz directly.\n- How answers become a bee's look: `public/js/bee-model.js` (`THEMES`, `designFromProfile`, `designFromQuiz`). See [docs/HANDOFF.md section 1.1](docs/HANDOFF.md#11-how-each-bee-gets-its-look).\n- Edit questions in `/admin`. See [Known issues](docs/HANDOFF.md#8-known-issues-and-next-steps) for content the client may want to review.\n\n## Brand\n\n- Colours, type and logo rules follow Factory International's *01 Guidelines_3rd party 2 1.pdf*.\n- The official Factory International logo (Third Party Use version) is in `public/img/` and is switched on in `public/img/logo.json`.\n- The Gräbenbach fonts are on (web licence confirmed) unless `BRAND_FONTS=off`. See [docs/HANDOFF.md section 6](docs/HANDOFF.md#6-the-real-logo-and-the-gräbenbach-fonts).\n"
+      "requirements": "# The Hive\n\nRun development, tests and deployment from this `BeeHive` folder. Backend code lives in `backend/hive/`. The separate Puzzle Punks repository, including its Git history, lives in `backend/puzzle-punks/`; `Documents/backend` is a shortcut to it. The older Hive app is preserved in a private archive under `_backups/consolidation-20261008/`. See [the consolidation notes](docs/CONSOLIDATION.md).\n\nThe Hive (working name Buzz TV) is a quiz game for Factory International's learning hub (Titus, on Moodle), where every learner grows a bee from their answers.\n\n1. **Build Your Bee.** The home page shows a starter bee and an editable, made-up name. Learners can keep that name or invent their own, then select **Next**. There are no skin unlocks or Random Bee option.\n2. **Discover Your Transferable Skills.** Selecting **Next** opens the first question of the 15-question career profile, with no category choice and no right or wrong answers. As learners answer, their bee grows on a retro TV. Its costume, prop, wing pattern, stripes and glow relate to their answers.\n3. **Join The Hive.** Their finished bee joins the live swarm shown full screen on a TV in the building. Playing again on the same device can rename and regrow the same bee, and the TV updates its name and design.\n\nBee names must have 2 to 24 Unicode characters, start with a letter, and use letters, digits, spaces, apostrophes or hyphens. The server validates and moderates them through `POST /api/bee-name` before the quiz starts, and checks them again before publication. Learners should invent names rather than use real names. Plays are anonymous, and Moodle does not send learner details to the Hive.\n\nOptional AI agents, written by Claude, switch on when `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is set: a **host bee** that comments on the Hive TV, a **career coach** with personal next steps on the results screen, **Draft with AI** for admins, and AI bees that fill the Hive while it has fewer than 30 real bees. Without a key, everything works with hand-written text. See [docs/HANDOFF.md section 9](docs/HANDOFF.md#9-the-ai-agents-claude).\n\n| Page | Live address | What it is |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/` | https://buzz-tv-six.vercel.app | The game. Moodle shows this, through the SCORM package or an iframe. |\n| `/tv` | https://buzz-tv-six.vercel.app/tv | The Hive TV. Open it full screen on the laptop connected to the TV. |\n| `/admin` | https://buzz-tv-six.vercel.app/admin | Admin: questions, bees, stats and admins. Log in with an email one-time link (approved emails only). |\n\n**Read the full hand-off guide: [docs/HANDOFF.md](docs/HANDOFF.md).** It covers admin how-tos, Moodle set-up, the Hive TV, the logo and fonts, deployment, the database, security and known issues. For step-by-step Totara and Moodle set-up, see [docs/LMS-SETUP.md](docs/LMS-SETUP.md). Content checks are in [docs/CONTENT-QA.md](docs/CONTENT-QA.md).\n\nProject tasks and requirements are in the [shared dashboard](https://roobsworld.com/dashboard). See [the task dashboard guide](docs/TASK-DASHBOARD.md) for direct AI API access and refresh commands.\n\n## How it's built\n\n- Plain Node 20+, with static HTML, CSS and JavaScript in `public/` (no build step). The only npm dependency is the official Anthropic SDK, for the optional AI bees.\n- One Vercel function (`api/index.js`, which uses `backend/hive/handler.js`) serves every `/api/*` route.\n- Supabase stores questions, bees, anonymous plays and admins. Only the server talks to it.\n- `npm run build:scorm` makes a small SCORM 1.2 launcher (`dist/the-hive-scorm12.zip`). It shows the live site inside Moodle and reports results.\n\n## Quick start for developers\n\n```bash\nnpm run dev          # http://localhost:3000 (game /, Hive TV /tv, admin /admin)\nnpm test             # Node test runner, in-memory data\nnpm run build:scorm  # dist/the-hive-scorm12.zip; add -- --pass 70 for pass/fail\n```\n\n- `npm run dev` explicitly enables disposable memory storage when neither Supabase setting is present. Hosted deployments and partial credentials fail closed with 503.\n- Admin login then returns a local dev token instead of emailing a link. Use `grindheadgames@gmail.com`, the built-in owner.\n- If `.env` has `SUPABASE_URL` and `SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY`, the local server uses that Supabase project instead.\n\nCopy `.env.example` to `.env` for the variable names. Their meanings are in [docs/HANDOFF.md section 7.4](docs/HANDOFF.md#74-environment-variables). Never commit `.env`.\n\n## Deploy\n\n```bash\nnpm run deploy\n```\n\nThis deploys the Hive to the existing Vercel project `buzz-tv`, using its configured production environment. Then check that `/api/health` shows `\"storage\":\"supabase\"`. To replace environment settings from `.env`, update Supabase login URLs and rebuild the SCORM package, use `bash scripts/deploy-now.sh`.\n\nFor a new database, run the SQL files in `supabase/` in this order: `01`, `03`, `02`, `04`, `05`, `06`, `07`, `08`, `09`, `10`, `11`. See [docs/HANDOFF.md section 7.6](docs/HANDOFF.md#76-database-set-up-and-migrations).\n\n## Content\n\nWebsite wording can be edited in a Google Sheet with `Header` and `Content` columns. The game, Hive TV, admin interface, quiz wording and results read the mapping through `/api/content`. See [the website text guide](docs/WEBSITE-TEXT.md) for connection settings, refresh behavior and adding new question rows.\n\n- The career quiz is the client's Creative Career Discovery content (`backend/hive/career-discovery-questions.json`), scored by `backend/hive/career.js`.\n- The four arts quizzes (Theatre, Music, Dance and Visual Art) are in `backend/hive/seed-data.js` and remain editable in admin and available through the API. The learner website shows the transferable skills quiz directly.\n- How answers become a bee's look: `public/js/bee-model.js` (`THEMES`, `designFromProfile`, `designFromQuiz`). See [docs/HANDOFF.md section 1.1](docs/HANDOFF.md#11-how-each-bee-gets-its-look).\n- Edit questions in `/admin`. See [Known issues](docs/HANDOFF.md#8-known-issues-and-next-steps) for content the client may want to review.\n\n## Brand\n\n- Colours, type and logo rules follow Factory International's *01 Guidelines_3rd party 2 1.pdf*.\n- The official Factory International logo (Third Party Use version) is in `public/img/` and is switched on in `public/img/logo.json`.\n- The Gr\u00e4benbach fonts are on (web licence confirmed) unless `BRAND_FONTS=off`. See [docs/HANDOFF.md section 6](docs/HANDOFF.md#6-the-real-logo-and-the-gr\u00e4benbach-fonts).\n"
