       "title": "Adding The Hive to Totara or Moodle",
-      "requirements": "# Adding The Hive to Totara or Moodle\n\nThis guide is for course administrators. It explains how to add The Hive to a Totara or Moodle course as a SCORM package, which settings to choose, what learners see, and what the LMS records.\n\nEverything marked **checked** below was tested with a stand-in LMS (see [How this was verified](#how-this-was-verified)). The LMS menu names were **not** checked in a real Moodle or Totara, so they may be worded slightly differently on your site.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Build the package\n\nA developer does this once. You only need a new package if the web address, the pass mark or the title changes. Editing questions never needs a new package.\n\n1. On a computer with the project and Node.js 20 or newer, open a terminal in the project folder.\n2. Run:\n\n   ```bash\n   npm run build:scorm\n   ```\n\n3. The package is saved as `dist/the-hive-scorm12.zip` (SCORM 1.2). It shows the live Hive website inside the LMS.\n\nOptions (add them after `--`):\n\n| What you want | Command |\n|---|---|\n| A pass mark for the arts quizzes (see note) | `npm run build:scorm -- --pass 70` |\n| A different web address | `npm run build:scorm -- https://hive.example.org` |\n| A different title in the LMS | `npm run build:scorm -- --title \"The Hive\"` |\n\n**Note on the pass mark.** At the moment, learners can only reach the **career quiz** (Discover Your Transferable Skills). The career quiz has no score, so a pass mark makes no difference to it. The four arts quizzes (Theatre, Music, Dance and Visual Art) are still in the system, and the package can record their scores, but learners have no way to open them from the game. If you build with `--pass`, choose **Completed** for completion (step 7 below), not **Passed**, or no learner will ever complete the activity.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Upload it as a SCORM activity\n\n1. Open the course and turn editing on.\n2. Select **Add an activity or resource**, then **SCORM package**.\n3. Enter a **Name**, for example \"The Hive\".\n4. Under **Package file**, upload `the-hive-scorm12.zip`.\n5. Set the options in section 3 below.\n6. Select **Save and display**.\n7. Try it with a test learner account (or **Log in as**) before telling learners. Play the career quiz to the results page, close the activity, then check the reports (section 5).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Recommended settings\n\nNames vary between Moodle versions, between Totara versions, and between the two. Where your site uses a different name, look for the setting with the same meaning.\n\n### Appearance\n\n1. **Display package**: **Current window** (recommended) or **New window**. Both were checked.\n   - **Current window**: the game appears in the course page. Allow at least **700 pixels of height**. If your site has **Width** and **Height** settings, set Width to 100% and Height to at least 700 pixels (more is better, see the note below).\n   - **New window** (Moodle may call it \"popup\"): set the window to at least **1000 × 750 pixels**. Learners must allow pop-ups for your LMS (see Troubleshooting).\n2. **Student skip content structure page** (Totara and older Moodle: \"Skip content structure page\"): **Always**. There is only one page, so the structure page adds nothing.\n3. **Display course structure in player** or **Display course structure on entry page**: **No** / **Hidden**.\n4. **Hide navigation buttons** (sometimes **Show navigation**): hide them. The game has its own buttons.\n\n**Screen size note (checked).** In a 1000 × 700 frame, the question and the first four answers are visible straight away, but learners scroll down a little inside the game to see the fifth answer and the **Next question** button. At 1000 × 750 they still scroll a little. The bee's TV is beside the questions at these sizes, never above them, and there is no sideways scrolling. On a phone-width screen (390 pixels) the TV is hidden while playing and learners scroll down for the later answers, which is normal on a phone.\n\n### Attempts management\n\n1. **Number of attempts**: **Unlimited**.\n2. **Attempts grading** (if shown): **Last completed attempt** or **Highest grade**. Neither matters much for the career quiz, which has no score.\n3. **Grading method**: **Learning objects** (the activity counts as 1 once completed) suits the career quiz. **Highest grade** only matters if the arts quizzes return.\n4. **Force new attempt**: **No**. The package keeps everything in one attempt: a learner who plays again adds more answer lines to the same attempt, and a \"passed\" result is never replaced by a lower one.\n5. **Lock after final attempt**: No.\n\n### Activity completion\n\n1. **Completion tracking**: **Show activity as complete when conditions are met**.\n2. Tick **Require status** (Moodle: **Students must receive a status**) and choose **Completed**.\n   - If you built with `--pass` and the arts quizzes are made available again, also tick **Passed**. Moodle treats either ticked status as complete.\n3. Do not use **Require minimum score** for the career quiz. It has no score.\n\n---\n\n## 4. What learners see\n\n1. The activity opens on the **Build Your Bee** page: a starter bee with a made-up name, a box to change the name, and a **Next** button. Learners should keep or invent a made-up name, never their real name.\n2. **Next** opens the first of the **15 career questions**. Each question has five answers (A to E), with no right or wrong answers. Learners can go back with **Previous** and change an answer.\n3. As they answer, their bee grows on a small TV beside the questions.\n4. After question 15 they see their results: their strongest creative pathway, suggested roles, a second pathway to explore and their top strengths. Their bee then joins the live Hive.\n5. Under the game there is a small link, **Open The Hive in a new window**. Anything played through that link is **not** recorded in the LMS. Tell learners to play inside the activity.\n6. The LMS records the activity as **incomplete** the moment the learner opens it, and **completed** as soon as the results page appears (checked). Learners do not need to do anything else.\n\n---\n\n## 5. What is recorded, and where to find it\n\nThe LMS never sends learner names or other details to The Hive.\n\n### Career quiz (checked)\n\n| Item | What is recorded |\n|---|---|\n| **Status** | **incomplete** on first opening, **completed** when the results page appears. If a \"passed\" was already recorded, it stays \"passed\". |\n| **Score** | None. The career quiz has no score. |\n| **Interactions** | 15 lines per play, one per question, for example `transferable-skills_q01`. Each shows the letter chosen (a to e), the type \"choice\" and the result \"neutral\". |\n| **Comments** | The learner's latest result, for example: \"Creative Career Discovery: Events & Live (Event Producer). Strengths: Planning & organisation, Collaboration & relationships, Communication & storytelling\". |\n| **Time** | How long the activity was open, added when the learner closes it. |\n\nThe letter recorded (a to e) refers to the answer's position in the original question list, not the shuffled order the learner saw. To see which answer a letter means, look up the question in `/admin`.\n\n### Arts quizzes (checked with a simulated result only, as learners cannot reach them)\n\n| Item | What would be recorded |\n|---|---|\n| **Score** | The percentage correct, 0 to 100. The best score is kept. |\n| **Status** | **completed**, or with `--pass`, **passed** or **failed**. A pass is never replaced by a fail. |\n| **Interactions** | One line per question with the learner's answer, the correct answer, and \"correct\" or \"wrong\". |\n\n### Where to find it\n\nExact menu names vary.\n\n1. **Moodle**: open the activity, then **Reports** (or the **Reports** tab). The **Basic report** lists each learner's attempts, status and time. Select an attempt to see every recorded value, including **cmi.comments**. The **Interactions report** lists the answer lines.\n2. **Totara**: open the activity, then **Reports** (or **Attempts**). Select a learner's attempt to see the tracked values, including comments and interactions.\n3. **Completion**: the course's **Activity completion** report shows who has completed the activity.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Carrying on later (resume)\n\nChecked:\n\n1. If a learner closes the activity part-way through the career quiz, the LMS keeps the attempt as **incomplete** and marked \"suspended\".\n2. When they open it again **on the same computer and in the same web browser**, within **2 hours**, the game offers **Carry on where you left off?** with the question number (for example \"question 6 of 15\"). **Carry on** takes them back to that question.\n3. When they finish, the attempt becomes **completed** as normal.\n\nLimits:\n\n- The place in the quiz is kept in the learner's web browser, not in the LMS. On another computer, another browser, a private window, or after clearing browser data, the game starts again from question 1 (checked). Nothing already recorded is lost.\n- After 2 hours, the saved place is dropped and the quiz starts again.\n- Some browsers block storage inside embedded content (see Troubleshooting). Then carrying on will not work, but recording still does.\n\n---\n\n## 7. The simpler alternative: a link or an embedded page\n\nYou can link to The Hive with a **URL** resource, or embed it in a **Page** with an iframe, for example:\n\n```html\n<iframe src=\"https://buzz-tv-six.vercel.app/\" title=\"The Hive\" style=\"width:100%;height:800px;border:0\" allow=\"fullscreen\"></iframe>\n```\n\nThis is simpler, but **the LMS records nothing**: no completion (other than \"viewed\", if you set that), no answers and no results. Use the SCORM package if you need records.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Troubleshooting\n\n### The activity shows a blank or grey frame\n\n1. Check that the live site opens on its own in a new tab. If it does not, the site is down or the address in the package is wrong.\n2. If the package was built for a different address (for example a test server), build it again with the right address and upload the new zip to the same activity.\n3. Your organisation's network or browser policy may block embedded content from other sites. Try **New window** display, or ask IT to allow the Hive's address.\n\n### Nothing is recorded\n\n1. Make sure the learner played **inside** the activity, not through **Open The Hive in a new window** or a separate tab.\n2. Make sure they reached the results page. Completion is recorded only when the results appear.\n3. Check that **Force new attempt** is **No**, and that the learner is not looking at an old attempt in **Review** mode. In review mode the LMS may not save anything new. Ask them to start the activity normally.\n4. Teachers and administrators previewing the activity may not be tracked. Test with a learner account.\n5. Ask the learner to close the activity with the LMS's own **Exit activity** button, or by closing the window, rather than leaving it open. The time spent and the \"suspended\" marker are saved when the activity closes. Completion itself is saved straight away.\n\n### \"Carry on\" is not offered, or the bee's name is forgotten\n\nSome browsers (notably Safari, and Firefox or Chrome with strict privacy settings) keep embedded sites' storage separate or block it altogether. This is sometimes called third-party storage or third-party cookies. The game still works and the LMS still records results, but learners may not be offered \"Carry on\", and their bee's name may not be remembered between visits. If this matters, ask learners to use the same browser each time, and to avoid private windows.\n\n### New window mode does nothing\n\nThe browser has probably blocked the pop-up. Learners should allow pop-ups for your LMS address (usually an icon at the right of the address bar), then select **Enter** (or **Launch**) again. If the LMS page that opened the window is closed or navigated away while the game is open, results may not reach the LMS. Keep the LMS page open until finished.\n\n### Learners have to scroll to see all the answers\n\nSince 8 October 2026 the game switches to a compact layout inside short frames, so all five answers and the **Next** button fit in a frame about 700 pixels tall. If learners still have to scroll, the frame is shorter than that: increase the activity's **Height** setting (at least 700 pixels), or use **New window**.\n\n---\n\n## How this was verified\n\nDocker was not available, so a real Moodle or Totara could not be installed for this test. Instead:\n\n- The package was built for a local copy of The Hive (`node scripts/build-scorm.js http://localhost:3931`, and again with `--pass 70`), running with test data only. The live site was not contacted.\n- A stand-in LMS page provided the SCORM 1.2 connection using the open-source **scorm-again** library (`Scorm12API`), logged every call and its result, and saved the learner's data between launches. The same tests were repeated with a stricter test connection that follows the SCORM 1.2 rules exactly (based on `tests/scorm-conformance.test.js`). No errors were reported by either.\n- The stand-in LMS and the game ran on different sites (`127.0.0.1` and `localhost`), so the browser treated the game as embedded content from another site, as it would in a real LMS.\n- Browsers: Chrome (all checks), Firefox and WebKit (Safari's engine) for the full career quiz at desktop size.\n- The arts quizzes cannot be opened by learners, so their results were simulated by sending a realistic result (built from a real arts round) from the game's own address.\n\nScreenshots and call logs are in `design-pass-7/lms/`, including:\n\n- First launch: `a-sa-first-launch.png`\n- Career quiz: `b-sa-question1.png`, `b-sa-results.png`, `b-firefox-sa-results.png`, `b-webkit-sa-results.png`, logs `b-sa-calls.log`, `b-strict-calls.log`\n- Arts results: logs `c-sa-pkg70-calls.log`, `c-sa-pkg0-calls.log`\n- Resume: `d-sa-after-5.png`, `d-sa-relaunch-resume-offer.png`, `d-sa-resumed-q6.png`, `d-other-device-no-resume.png`\n- Display: `e-frame-1000x700-q1.png`, `e-frame-1000x700-q2-picked.png`, `e-newwindow-1000x750-q1.png`, `e-phone-390x844-q1.png`, `e-phone-390x844-results.png`\n- Playing again: `f-sa-calls.log`\n\nWhat still needs checking in a real Moodle or Totara is listed in the test report: menu names, the reports pages, review mode, and storage in Safari.\n\n## Current automated verification — 11 October 2026\n\nThe retained `tests/browser/scorm-launcher.spec.js` builds the ZIP, serves its actual launcher inside a disposable LMS course on `127.0.0.1`, and embeds the quiz from `localhost`. All six cases passed across Chromium, Firefox and WebKit at desktop and phone widths. Each leaves after five answers, checks suspend, reopens the same browser context, resumes the final ten answers, and verifies completion, 15 neutral choice interactions, no numeric score, commit, session time and finish. The local backend uses fixture storage and no production credentials. All 105 Node regression tests also passed, including strict SCORM API conformance.\n\nEvidence and package digest: `docs/evidence/2026-10-11-scorm-cross-site.json`. The current upload artifact is `../portfolio/output/task-fixes/beehive-lms/the-hive-scorm12.zip`, pointing at `https://buzz-tv-six.vercel.app`. This verifies the launcher integration, while client Titus/Moodle upload, report pages, review mode and physical Safari storage acceptance remain pending.\n"
