-      "requirements": "# Content QA: The Hive\n\nDate: 2026-10-07. Scope: `backend/hive/seed-data.js` (4 arts quizzes x 20 questions, discipline blurbs), `backend/hive/career-discovery-questions.json` (15 questions), `backend/hive/career.js` (PATHWAYS label/blurb/about), learner-facing strings in `public/js/game.js`, `public/index.html`, `public/tv.html`, `public/js/tv.js`, `scorm/index.html`. Also glanced at the option labels in `public/js/bee-model.js`.\n\n## (a) Typos fixed\n\n**None.** I found no clear typos, misspellings, US spellings or grammar slips in any file in scope, so no files were edited. The live database copy needs no matching changes.\n\nChecks run: a full read of every file, plus a pattern search for US spellings (color/colors, center, theater, organize, program, gray, favor, honor, license and so on), doubled words, stray spaces before commas, and `...` used instead of `…`. UK spellings are used throughout (colour, organisation, programme, visualising, prioritising, formalised, gelatine, make-up). The ellipsis character (…) and arrows are consistent.\n\n| File | Old text | New text |\n|---|---|---|\n| (none) | | |\n\n## (b) Factual corrections approved and applied, 10 October 2026\n\n| # | Quiz / question | Issue | Suggested fix |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Theatre: \"What do theatre people traditionally say to wish an actor good luck?\" | \"Knock them dead\" is also a common way to wish a performer luck, so two options could be seen as right. | Replace the distractor \"Knock them dead\" with something clearly wrong, such as \"Chin up\". |\n| 2 | Dance: \"Capoeira, which blends dance and martial arts, comes from which country?\" | The distractor \"Angola\" is risky. Capoeira grew from Central African (often described as Angolan) traditions brought by enslaved people, and the fact itself mentions enslaved Africans. A learner could argue for Angola. | Replace \"Angola\" with a clearly unrelated country, such as \"Portugal\" or \"Mexico\". |\n| 3 | Visual Art: \"Who painted 'The Starry Night'?\" (fact) | The fact says Van Gogh painted it \"from his window\". He painted it in his studio from memory and sketches of the view from his bedroom window, not at the window. | \"Van Gogh painted it in 1889, based on the view from his window at an asylum in Saint-Rémy.\" |\n| 4 | Music: \"Which city did The Beatles come from?\" (fact) | \"The band formed in Liverpool in 1960\" is broadly right: they took the name The Beatles in 1960. But the group grew out of the Quarrymen (1957), so some sources date its forming earlier. | \"The band took the name The Beatles in Liverpool in 1960.\" |\n| 5 | Theatre: \"Who usually calls the lighting and sound cues during a show?\" (fact) | Low priority. In UK theatre the deputy stage manager (DSM) usually calls the show. The fact's \"(or deputy)\" covers this, but the UK convention could be clearer. | \"In UK theatres this is usually the deputy stage manager (DSM), working from the prompt desk.\" |\n| 6 | Visual Art: \"What is the complementary colour of blue?\" | Low priority. Orange is right in traditional (red, yellow, blue) colour theory. In light and screen colour (RGB), blue's complement is yellow. Yellow is not one of the options, so the answer is not ambiguous. | Optionally start the question with \"In traditional colour theory,\" to match the primary-colours question. |\n\nAll six suggestions above were explicitly approved on 10 October 2026 and applied to bundled content, seed SQL and the production database. A targeted migration preserves unrelated admin edits. Production verification found all six corrected questions.\n\nI checked every other marked answer and fact and found no problems (see (d)).\n\n## (c) Style and plain-language suggestions (not applied)\n\n1. **Welcome screen (`game.js`):** \"Pick a colour, stripes, wings and a hat.\" The Accessory group also offers glasses, a bow, headphones and so on, not only hats. Suggest \"Pick a colour, stripes, wings and an accessory\" (or \"...and something to wear\").\n2. **Builder note (`game.js`):** \"Locked skins unlock when you finish a quiz in that discipline.\" \"Discipline\" is slightly jargon-y. Suggest \"...when you finish that arts quiz.\"\n3. **Transferable-skills blurb (`seed-data.js`):** \"Find the creative careers the skills you already have could lead to.\" This is grammatical but hard to read. Suggest \"See which creative careers your skills could lead to.\"\n4. **\"The Hive\" vs \"the Hive\":** the capitalisation varies. Mid-sentence it is mostly \"the Hive\" (index strap, game messages, \"Join the Hive\"), but `tv.html` has \"every bee built in The Hive\" and the QR label \"opens The Hive\", and `scorm/index.html` has \"Open The Hive\". The same goes for \"Hive TV\" (\"Watch the Hive TV\" vs title \"The Hive TV\"). Suggest a house rule, for example \"The Hive\" for the product name and \"the Hive\" for the place where bees gather, then apply it everywhere.\n5. **SCORM link (`scorm/index.html`):** the visible text \"Open The Hive in a new window\" contradicts its hidden screen-reader text \"(opens in a new tab)\". Suggest \"Open The Hive in a new tab\".\n6. **Repeated content:** Music (\"How many beats are in a bar of 3/4 time?\", fact about waltzes) and Dance (\"A waltz is usually danced in which time signature?\") test the same fact. Consider replacing one.\n7. **Woodcut fact (Visual Art):** \"Ink sits on the raised surface left after carving, which is then pressed onto paper.\" It is unclear what \"which\" refers to. Suggest \"After carving, ink is rolled onto the raised surface and the block is pressed onto paper.\"\n8. **Tango option (Dance):** \"Argentina & Uruguay\" uses an ampersand. \"Argentina and Uruguay\" reads more plainly, especially for screen readers.\n9. **Career quiz prompts (client content, leave unless the client agrees):** the question stems vary (\"What are you particularly good at?\", \"Which are you particularly good at?\", \"Which part are you particularly good at?\", \"Which would you be strongest at?\"). That is fine, but the client may want to standardise them.\n10. **Index note:** the hard-coded domain \"buzz-tv-six.vercel.app\" in the loading fallback will need updating if the site moves to a Factory International domain.\n\n## (d) Checked and fine\n\nI checked all 80 arts questions (prompt, 4 options, the marked `answer` and the `fact`), the 15 career questions (including the drafted Q15 option E), all 7 PATHWAYS labels, blurbs and about texts, and every visible string in game.js, index.html, tv.html, tv.js and scorm/index.html. Spelling, UK English, grammar and punctuation are clean. Every marked answer is correct, and exactly one option is clearly correct in every arts question except the two flagged in (b) #1 and #2. Facts are accurate apart from the minor wording points in (b). The tone is consistently friendly and plain.\n"
