-      "requirements": "# Website text in Google Sheets\n\nEdit [The Hive website text](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1NqOsu2_7PbYGa8cVgoDIGsGFWB0PfG-lqxIhT2nkyK0/edit). The workbook contains the current website copy, database questions and bundled outage content. Local `.env` and Vercel Production are configured to read this Sheet.\n\nVerified on 10 October 2026: the public website reports `source: \"google-sheets\"`, `configured: true`, and no missing or unknown keys. All six approved question corrections appear in both database and offline wording rows. The 42 newer interface labels were added using their existing application wording. See `docs/evidence/2026-10-10-content-sheet.json` for the deployment and checks.\n\nThe `Website text` tab contains one row per editable text key. Its first four columns are `Header`, `Content`, `Page` and `Location`. Edit `Content`; keep `Header` unchanged. Headings, body copy, buttons, messages, accessibility labels, quiz names, questions, answer options, explanations, career results and result cards use this mapping.\n\nThe `Header` column identifies the text. For example, `game.welcome.heading` changes the welcome heading and `question.<id>.option.1` changes the first answer of that question. A key shared by repeated uses of the same label updates every use. Quiz question IDs, answer positions and scoring tags stay in the application. Editing wording does not alter scoring or bee traits.\n\nKeep placeholders such as `{name}`, `{count}`, `{number}` and `{total}` where the text needs a learner's name or a current number. Content is plain text. HTML is displayed as text and never executed. An empty Content cell deliberately hides that label. A missing row uses the bundled wording. Duplicate keys or invalid column headers reject that refresh and retain the last valid copy.\n\nLearner names, counts, scores, URLs and other live data still come from the application. The spreadsheet controls the labels and sentences around them. Bundled question rows are included alongside database rows for quizzes served during a database outage.\n\n## Connect the Sheet\n\nSet `GOOGLE_SHEETS_SPREADSHEET_ID` to the ID between `/d/` and `/edit` in the Sheet URL. The default range is `'Website text'!A1:B5000`. The website reads the first two columns and ignores the explanatory columns.\n\nChoose one access method:\n\n- Share the Sheet as **Anyone with the link / Viewer** for public website wording. The server reads its CSV from Google without an API key. Editing still requires your Google account.\n- Keep the Sheet private. Enable the Google Sheets API in a Google Cloud project, create a service account, share the Sheet with its `client_email` as Viewer, and set `GOOGLE_SHEETS_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON` to its complete JSON key. Keep this setting only on the server.\n- A public-read Sheet can also use `GOOGLE_SHEETS_API_KEY` with the Sheets API.\n\nFor local development, put these settings in `.env` and restart `npm run dev`. For the live site, set them in the existing Vercel project's environment and deploy the code. The website's Google Drive connection in Codex is used to create the Sheet; the deployed server needs one of the read methods above.\n\nGoogle's [Sheets values API](https://developers.google.com/workspace/sheets/api/reference/rest/v4/spreadsheets.values/get) and [service account guide](https://developers.google.com/identity/protocols/oauth2/service-account) describe the private read method.\n\n## Refresh and verify\n\nThe server checks Google at most once per minute. Reload the game or admin page to read fresh wording. The unattended TV checks every minute. An outage uses the last valid copy in that running server instance, or the bundled copy after a cold start.\n\n`GET /api/content` reports `source`, `configured`, `updatedAt`, `missingHeaders` and `unknownHeaders`. `source: \"google-sheets\"` confirms a successful read; `\"cached\"` means the latest read failed and the server retained the last valid copy; `\"defaults\"` means bundled text is active. Admins can call `GET /api/admin/content/export` with their session token to obtain the complete current catalog.\n\nWhen adding a question in the admin portal, add its new catalog rows to the Sheet. Rows are keyed by question ID, so reordering questions does not move their wording to a different question. Removing a question leaves its old Sheet rows unused. Admin question forms continue to edit the stored questions and scoring; spreadsheet wording takes precedence on the learner pages. Refresh the catalog after adding or changing content that needs new keys.\n\nStatic HTML retains bundled fallback text for script-disabled browsers and while modules are loading. SCORM launchers built from the updated source receive their labels from the live game. Rebuild and upload the SCORM package to update an older launcher.\n"
