inute. Reload the game or admin page to read fresh wording. The unattended TV checks every minute. An outage uses the last valid copy in that running server instance, or the bundled copy after a cold start.\n\n`GET /api/content` reports `source`, `configured`, `updatedAt`, `missingHeaders` and `unknownHeaders`. `source: \"google-sheets\"` confirms a successful read; `\"cached\"` means the latest read failed and the server retained the last valid copy; `\"defaults\"` means bundled text is active. Admins can call `GET /api/admin/content/export` with their session token to obtain the complete current catalog.\n\nWhen adding a question in the admin portal, add its new catalog rows to the Sheet. Rows are keyed by question ID, so reordering questions does not move their wording to a different question. Removing a question leaves its old Sheet rows unused. Admin question forms continue to edit the stored questions and scoring; spreadsheet wording takes precedence on the learner pages. Refresh the catalog after adding or changing content that needs new keys.\n\nStatic HTML retains bundled fallback text for script-disabled browsers and while modules are loading. SCORM launchers built from the updated source receive their labels from the live game. Rebuild and upload the SCORM package to update an older launcher.\n"
