       "title": "Central tasks and requirements",
-      "requirements": "# Central tasks and requirements\n\nThe central dashboard for Bee, Portfolio and dashboard work is https://roobsworld.com/dashboard. It requires an authorized admin login. Other repositories remain available in the inventory.\n\nAI tools use the authenticated, read-only API:\n\n```sh\ncurl --fail --silent --show-error \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPERATIONS_API_TOKEN\" \\\n  'https://roobsworld.com/api/operations?project=Grindhead%2Fthe-hive'\n```\n\nThe server-only API credential is managed in Portfolio; do not put it in URLs or browser code. Responses include tasks, requirement documents, source paths, priorities, acceptance criteria and evidence dates. Reads do not execute checks or change task state.\n\nRefresh from `../portfolio` using `node scripts/sync-operations-local.mjs`, verify the register and deploy Portfolio. `BEEHIVE_ROOT` overrides the default sibling BeeHive path. Snapshot imports must be republished after source changes. Existing resolution receipts are checked against current file hashes; stale receipts require verification.\n\nThe older Riddle Quest release dashboard is retained as a historical report. Publish new Bee progress to the central register above.\n\n## Verified resolutions\n\n`docs/task-resolutions.json` records completed work, remaining dependencies, verification checks and SHA-256 digests of the source files that were checked. Dashboard sync uses these receipts and changes completed work back to Verification pending if its source files change.\n\nThe 10 October 2026 release completed shared limits, final-owner protection, the deployment wizard, the approved daily 365-day purge, the confirmed owner list and six approved arts corrections. The configured production content Sheet is verified. AI remains blocked until an approved Anthropic key is configured. Client LMS rollout and the authored career additions still need client acceptance.\n\nRun the database integration checks without retaining any fixture changes:\n\n```bash\nnode --env-file=.env scripts/database-query.js supabase/tests/operational_safeguards.sql\n```\n\nThe helper reads the local Supabase access token without printing it. This integration check always rolls back its fixture transaction.\n\nThe 11 October creative-area change has 33 passing Chromium/Firefox/WebKit TV and complete career-flow scenarios plus hosted WebKit evidence in `docs/CREATIVE-HIVE-AREAS.md`. Bee task declarations in `docs/development-tasks/*.json` are imported alongside the historical tracker, with the same receipt hash checks.\n"
