       "id": "Grindhead/the-hive:docs/RELIABILITY-FIXES.md",
       "project": "Grindhead/the-hive",
       "source": "docs/RELIABILITY-FIXES.md",
-      "title": "Bee reliability fixes — 10 October 2026",
-      "requirements": "# Bee reliability fixes — 10 October 2026\n\nHosted production and preview deployments require both Supabase settings. Disposable storage is available only through explicit `HIVE_LOCAL_MODE=true` in local development; the local server opts in. Partial credentials always fail closed.\n\nParsed and streamed request bodies use the same object-only validation and 50,000-byte UTF-8 limit. Quiz edits validate the merged answer and options, including edits that only change the answer or shrink the option list.\n\nSupabase data and authentication requests have a five-second connection-and-body deadline. `SUPABASE_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS` can set an integer from 10 to 15,000 milliseconds. Read outages can serve bundled questions; writes fail without automatic retries.\n\nThe game generates a random secret submission key for each finished round and reuses the exact payload when retrying. `11_retry_safe_bees.sql` commits the bee, quiz play and cached response together. Concurrent retries return the same bee and edit key; key reuse with another payload returns 409. The server retains only hashed capabilities. Retry receipts are service-only, RLS-protected, and removed when their bee is deleted. Older API callers can omit the key, but cannot recover a lost response without supplying a stable key.\n\nVerification: `npm test` exercises 96 regressions. `supabase/tests/retry-safe-bees.sql` verifies retry identity, one play, rollback on play failure, ownership, RLS and grants in a rollback transaction. `supabase/tests/operational_safeguards.sql` verifies the existing owner, limiter and retention protections.\n"
+      "title": "Bee reliability fixes \u2014 10 October 2026",
+      "requirements": "# Bee reliability fixes \u2014 10 October 2026\n\nHosted production and preview deployments require both Supabase settings. Disposable storage is available only through explicit `HIVE_LOCAL_MODE=true` in local development; the local server opts in. Partial credentials always fail closed.\n\nParsed and streamed request bodies use the same object-only validation and 50,000-byte UTF-8 limit. Quiz edits validate the merged answer and options, including edits that only change the answer or shrink the option list.\n\nSupabase data and authentication requests have a five-second connection-and-body deadline. `SUPABASE_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS` can set an integer from 10 to 15,000 milliseconds. Read outages can serve bundled questions; writes fail without automatic retries.\n\nThe game generates a random secret submission key for each finished round and reuses the exact payload when retrying. `11_retry_safe_bees.sql` commits the bee, quiz play and cached response together. Concurrent retries return the same bee and edit key; key reuse with another payload returns 409. The server retains only hashed capabilities. Retry receipts are service-only, RLS-protected, and removed when their bee is deleted. Older API callers can omit the key, but cannot recover a lost response without supplying a stable key.\n\nVerification: `npm test` exercises 96 regressions. `supabase/tests/retry-safe-bees.sql` verifies retry identity, one play, rollback on play failure, ownership, RLS and grants in a rollback transaction. `supabase/tests/operational_safeguards.sql` verifies the existing owner, limiter and retention protections.\n"
     },
