       "id": "Grindhead/the-hive:docs/CREATIVE-HIVE-AREAS.md",
       "project": "Grindhead/the-hive",
       "source": "docs/CREATIVE-HIVE-AREAS.md",
       "title": "Creative Hive areas",
-      "requirements": "# Creative Hive areas\n\nThe client feedback dated 7 October 2026 asks for bees to join creative areas that match their discovered transferable skills after the quiz. The requirement was missing from the central register.\n\nSource: [client feedback thread](https://mail.google.com/mail/u/?authuser=craigbeswetherick%40gmail.com#all/1a115fc5796177d0). Only this product requirement is retained here.\n\nThe strongest pathway already persists in `design.theme`. Seven labeled areas use the existing pathway names; older arts bees and bees without a current pathway stay in the general Hive. The result screen shows the learner alongside current Hive bees and highlights their name. The live Hive uses the same grouping. A pathway change moves the existing bee into its new area; a name-only poll keeps its element and position. Resizing and quiet-Hive scaling fit bees and captions inside their areas. Pause and reduced motion remain supported.\n\n## Verification\n\n105 Node tests pass. All 33 automated scenarios pass in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit. The browsers cover four TV viewports (320, 390, 1280 and 1920 pixels) and three complete career-flow viewports (320, 390 and 1280 pixels), including all 15 questions, reload/resume, results and replay. All learner writes are to a disposable local memory store. No production learners were created for these checks.\n\nThe earlier WebKit navigation failure came from VS Code Snap's inherited `GIO_MODULE_DIR`, not an application assertion. Removing only that override made the unchanged scenario pass. The browser configuration now removes it only for the VS Code Snap path, and the normal `npm run test:browser` command passes all engines. Diagnosis and current-source receipt: `docs/evidence/2026-10-11-webkit-navigation.json`. Physical Safari and the client's LMS remain separate acceptance gates.\n\nLocal receipts: `docs/evidence/2026-10-11-creative-hive-tv.json` and `docs/evidence/2026-10-11-creative-hive-results.json`. Staged source hashes and healthy Supabase storage passed before promotion. The canonical Hive deployment `dpl_4CXUAkogZFFXkiYvqTxjpqhiVvBa` passes the eight Chromium/Firefox TV viewport checks. Hosted receipt: `docs/evidence/2026-10-11-creative-hive-hosted.json`. Hosted WebKit also passes all four TV viewports; eight deployed asset hashes match the checked source. The probe used synthetic Hive responses and blocked every POST, including the normal seed request, so it made no production learner writes. Receipt: `docs/evidence/2026-10-11-creative-hive-webkit-hosted.json`. Physical Safari and the client LMS remain unverified.\n"
+      "requirements": "# Creative Hive areas\n\nCurrent acceptance update, 13 October 2026: the owner confirmed client approval of the seven authored pathway descriptions and waived physical Safari testing. The owner requested continued use of the current demo and deferred final-location rollout. Target deployment and LMS acceptance are deferred until rollout is requested and access is granted; earlier verification paragraphs below retain their historical scope. See `docs/evidence/2026-10-13-client-acceptance-update.json`.\nThe client feedback dated 7 October 2026 asks for bees to join creative areas that match their discovered transferable skills after the quiz. The requirement was missing from the central register.\n\nSource: [client feedback thread](https://mail.google.com/mail/u/?authuser=craigbeswetherick%40gmail.com#all/1a115fc5796177d0). Only this product requirement is retained here.\n\nThe strongest pathway already persists in `design.theme`. Seven labeled areas use the existing pathway names; older arts bees and bees without a current pathway stay in the general Hive. The result screen shows the learner alongside current Hive bees and highlights their name. The live Hive uses the same grouping. A pathway change moves the existing bee into its new area; a name-only poll keeps its element and position. Resizing and quiet-Hive scaling fit bees and captions inside their areas. Pause and reduced motion remain supported.\n\n## Verification\n\n105 Node tests pass. All 33 automated scenarios pass in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit. The browsers cover four TV viewports (320, 390, 1280 and 1920 pixels) and three complete career-flow viewports (320, 390 and 1280 pixels), including all 15 questions, reload/resume, results and replay. All learner writes are to a disposable local memory store. No production learners were created for these checks.\n\nThe earlier WebKit navigation failure came from VS Code Snap's inherited `GIO_MODULE_DIR`, not an application assertion. Removing only that override made the unchanged scenario pass. The browser configuration now removes it only for the VS Code Snap path, and the normal `npm run test:browser` command passes all engines. Diagnosis and current-source receipt: `docs/evidence/2026-10-11-webkit-navigation.json`. Physical Safari and the client's LMS remain separate acceptance gates.\n\nLocal receipts: `docs/evidence/2026-10-11-creative-hive-tv.json` and `docs/evidence/2026-10-11-creative-hive-results.json`. Staged source hashes and healthy Supabase storage passed before promotion. The canonical Hive deployment `dpl_4CXUAkogZFFXkiYvqTxjpqhiVvBa` passes the eight Chromium/Firefox TV viewport checks. Hosted receipt: `docs/evidence/2026-10-11-creative-hive-hosted.json`. Hosted WebKit also passes all four TV viewports; eight deployed asset hashes match the checked source. The probe used synthetic Hive responses and blocked every POST, including the normal seed request, so it made no production learner writes. Receipt: `docs/evidence/2026-10-11-creative-hive-webkit-hosted.json`. Physical Safari and the client LMS remain unverified.\n"
     },
     {
       "id": "Grindhead/the-hive:docs/TRANSFERABLE-SKILLS-QUIZ-V1.md",
       "project": "Grindhead/the-hive",
       "source": "docs/TRANSFERABLE-SKILLS-QUIZ-V1.md",
       "title": "Transferable Skills Quiz V1 workload",
-      "requirements": "# Transferable Skills Quiz V1 workload\n\nAdded 12 October 2026 from the user-supplied V1 Transferable Skills Quiz Content.pdf. Source SHA-256: `df002d7f662e8399cbec2abd0e6c053d6143327fa455601ece86205f11a4535b`. The original is retained privately in the Portfolio workspace at `output/task-fixes/beehive-transferable-skills/source.pdf`.\n\nThe user's request is to add this document to the workload. Document wording supplies proposed product requirements; it does not authorise deployment, client approval, or changing approved copy by itself.\n\n## Proposed scope\n\nIntegrate the 15-question Creative Career Discovery Quiz into BeeHive. Preserve authored question and answer wording after content clarification. Each question has five options, so the intended dataset contains 75 options. Score directly against creative pathways, with 2 points for a primary pathway, 1 for a relevant secondary pathway, and 1 for one or more roles within the primary pathway. Hide pathway and role tags while answering.\n\nShow the strongest pathway, strongest role within that pathway, a secondary role/pathway, and transferable strengths evidenced by selected answers. Present 2-4 relevant roles with the suggested wording “You could explore…”. Connect the strongest pathway to the existing creative Hive areas without changing already-approved content until this V1 content is confirmed.\n\n## Content and scoring clarifications\n\n- The introduction says seven pathways but enumerates six. Digital & Creative Technology appears in answer tags and needs a confirmed place in the canonical seven-pathway list.\n- Question 15E stops at “I found a new way of using technology or” and has no pathway or role tags. Obtain its complete wording and tags before publishing.\n- Several answers contain multiple pathway tags, including three tags. Confirm which is primary, how secondary points apply, and normalise aliases such as Film & TV / Film & TV Production, Marketing / Content, Digital, Theatre, and Creative.\n- Confirm role identifiers, which listed roles receive the point, tie-breaking and the transferable-strength explanations. Do not invent these authoring decisions or randomise tied results.\n\n## Work sequence and acceptance\n\n1. Confirm content and scoring gaps with the content owner. Record the approved wording, canonical pathways, role mappings and tie rules.\n2. Add a versioned question bank containing all 15 questions and 75 complete options with reviewed pathway/role tags. Retain provenance and validate completeness.\n3. Implement deterministic pathway and role scoring. Verify primary/secondary weights, multi-tag answers, ties, invalid/incomplete submissions and result explanations using realistic response sets.\n4. Integrate the quiz and results into BeeHive, preserving answer persistence, back navigation, replay, editable names and existing Hive grouping. Keep internal tags hidden during the quiz and show accessible result content.\n5. Verify browser and LMS delivery: keyboard and screen reader labels, narrow/wide layouts, reduced motion, reload/relaunch persistence and SCORM packaging. Record client content acceptance and actual target LMS acceptance separately from automated tests.\n\nThe standalone scoring module is implemented at `backend/hive/transferable-skills-scoring.js`. It requires an explicitly approved bank with source provenance, seven canonical pathways, all 15 questions and 75 complete choices, primary/secondary and primary-scoped role mappings, authored strength labels, and complete tie orders. It returns ranked scores with the selected question/choice evidence. It rejects the PDF-derived draft and does not fill unchosen roles or assign missing authoring decisions. Production integration, content approval and acceptance remain unfinished. Existing career-copy client review and creative-Hive-area tasks remain separate; this new workload does not mark them complete.\n\n## Reviewable proposal\n\nThe complete proposed wording and scoring mappings are in [the V1 review pack](TRANSFERABLE-SKILLS-QUIZ-V1-REVIEW.md). All 74 complete PDF options match the existing authored content after whitespace normalisation. The proposed completion for Question 15E comes from existing authored copy, where it is marked as drafted. The machine-readable bank remains `draft-for-review`; no client approval or production integration is claimed. Scoring verification is recorded in `docs/evidence/transferable-skills-scoring-2026-10-12.json`. All 114 Node regressions, including nine V1 scoring checks, pass.\n\n## Approved content decision\n\nThe user approved the complete reviewed proposal for implementation on 12 October 2026. The approval includes the Q15E completion, Digital & Creative Technology as the seventh pathway, all explicit scoring/strength mappings and the proposed tie orders. The approved versioned bank is `docs/content/transferable-skills-quiz-v1.json`; the source-bound approval receipt is `docs/evidence/transferable-skills-v1-content-approval-2026-10-12.json`. The original PDF-derived draft and proposed review pack remain as provenance. Integration and browser/LMS verification are still pending.\n\n## Verified implementation\n\nThe approved bank, server scorer, result evidence and creative Hive integration are deployed at https://buzz-tv-six.vercel.app. All 120 Node tests, 45 browser scenarios and nine additional V1 keyboard/evidence/persistence scenarios pass. Hosted read-only checks confirm exact approved copy, the V1 scoring version, reviewed tie orders, durable storage and matching frontend assets. The original question IDs remain usable for saved progress. The client LMS and physical Safari acceptance gates remain open; see `docs/evidence/transferable-skills-v1-verified-2026-10-12/` for verification evidence.\n"
+      "requirements": "# Transferable Skills Quiz V1 workload\n\nCurrent acceptance update, 13 October 2026: the owner confirmed client approval of the seven authored pathway descriptions and waived physical Safari testing. The owner requested continued use of the current demo and deferred final-location rollout. Target deployment and LMS acceptance are deferred until rollout is requested and access is granted; earlier verification paragraphs below retain their historical scope. See `docs/evidence/2026-10-13-client-acceptance-update.json`.\n\nAdded 12 October 2026 from the user-supplied V1 Transferable Skills Quiz Content.pdf. Source SHA-256: `df002d7f662e8399cbec2abd0e6c053d6143327fa455601ece86205f11a4535b`. The original is retained privately in the Portfolio workspace at `output/task-fixes/beehive-transferable-skills/source.pdf`.\n\n## Current status\n\nThe user approved the reviewed V1 proposal on 12 October 2026. The approved question bank, deterministic scorer, results and creative Hive integration are deployed at https://buzz-tv-six.vercel.app. Content confirmation, the question bank, scoring and results integration are complete. Automated browser and SCORM checks are verified. Target LMS acceptance is deferred to final rollout; physical Safari testing is waived.\n\nThe approval receipt is `docs/evidence/transferable-skills-v1-content-approval-2026-10-12.json`. Current task receipts and their source hashes are in `docs/task-resolutions.json`. The owner confirmed client approval of the seven authored pathway descriptions on 13 October 2026.\n\nThe original request added the PDF to the workload. The proposal and authoring gaps below describe the scope before the recorded approval.\n\n## Original proposed scope\n\nIntegrate the 15-question Creative Career Discovery Quiz into BeeHive. Preserve authored question and answer wording after content clarification. Each question has five options, so the intended dataset contains 75 options. Score directly against creati